  "hindi": "आज कौन पौरुषवान्, देवों को चाहने वाला, कामना करता हुआ, इन्द्र की मित्रता में आनन्दित हुआ है? अथवा सोम निचोड़कर, अग्नि के प्रज्वलित होने पर, कौन महान् सहायता के लिए, पार पहुँचाने के लिए स्तुति करता है?",
  "english": "Who today, manly, desiring the gods, wishing, has taken delight in Indra's friendship? Or who, having pressed Soma, with Agni kindled, praises for great help, for bringing across?",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "Printed īṭṭe is the Vedic spelling of īḍe (ṭṭ for ḍ before the ending); words give īḍe. pāryāya (dat., 'for bringing across / for carrying through') is taken as a dative of purpose; the exact form and sense are not certain. jujoṣa is a perfect with present sense. The object of īḍe is not stated in the verse.",
  "confidence": "medium"
 },
